Chain: Feature

Purpose:
  The full stage sequence for developing new functionality. Other chain
  types (see templates/bugfix.sdd, templates/change.sdd) reference this
  file's stage names rather than redefining them (see architecture/
  architecture.sdd -> NoDuplication).

Sequence:
  AN -> AR -> DB -> BE -> API -> FE -> MD -> QA -> DO -> VR

Stages:

  AN: Analysis
    meaning: Initial scope/requirement analysis — determine what the
      feature actually requires before any implementation stage begins
      (see chains.sdd -> Stages -> chain-orchestration stages).

  AR: Architecture
    meaning: Architecture decisions for the new work — what components,
      contracts and data shapes it introduces, before any discipline
      stage starts building them (see chains.sdd -> Stages ->
      chain-orchestration stages).

  DB  -> @../stages/DB.sdd
  BE  -> @../stages/BE.sdd
  API -> @../stages/API.sdd
  FE  -> @../stages/FE.sdd
  MD  -> @../stages/MD.sdd
  QA  -> @../stages/QA.sdd
  DO  -> @../stages/DO.sdd
  VR  -> @../stages/VR.sdd

Rules:
  [F1] Every stage requires its predecessor in Sequence to be complete
       before it may start (see chains.sdd -> Rules [C5]).
  [F2] Not every stage is mandatory for every feature — e.g. MD/DO may
       not apply (see chains.sdd -> Rules [C7]/[C9]; stages/MD.sdd ->
       Optional, stages/DO.sdd -> Optional). This file does not encode
       the per-feature activation condition — that is resolved by the
       chain execution mechanism, not hardcoded here.

State: +

Note:
  (prompt/new/33.md, STEP 11) Supersedes ../feature.chain (STEP 5),
  which is deleted in this same pass (preserved in git history — same
  precedent as STEP 5's deletion of the old _TEMPLATE.feature.sdd).

  Deliberate departures from the old feature.chain, applied per the
  standing "apply, don't copy" rule:

  Discipline stages (DB/BE/API/FE/MD/QA/DO/VR) are no longer redefined
  inline (old feature.chain repeated `name: X` for every stage) — they
  are now referenced from ./stages/*.sdd, defined once (see
  NoDuplication). AN/AR remain defined inline here, since they are
  chain-orchestration stages specific to this chain type (see
  chains.sdd -> Stages).

  Sequence arrows changed from bare `>` (old feature.chain) to `->`,
  matching the convention established in chains.sdd/state.sdd — `>`
  collides with the NEXT state transition symbol (see PROJECT.sdd ->
  State işarələri).

  Content translated from the original Azerbaijani (old feature.chain)
  into English — this anticipates, rather than contradicts, the
  still-pending repo-wide translation pass.
